From: arch-port <26345330+DrShadow34@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wayland/touch: Skip cancelled touches when looking up grab sequences

meta_wayland_touch_cancel() clears the focus surface of every live touch
but keeps the touch info until the sequence ends, serial included. A
client asking for a move / resize (xdg_toplevel.move) with the serial of
such a touch - Firefox does when a touch drag on its tab bar ends up in a
compositor grab - made touch_can_grab_surface() dereference the NULL
focus surface: gnome-shell segfaulted
(meta_wayland_seat_get_grab_info -> meta_wayland_touch_find_grab_sequence).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013fD3if93WntovhmD8fGa8C
---
--- a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-touch.c
+++ b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-touch.c
@@ -690,7 +690,11 @@
   while (g_hash_table_iter_next (&iter, (gpointer*) &sequence,
                                  (gpointer*) &touch_info))
     {
+      /* A cancelled touch (meta_wayland_touch_cancel(), e.g. a compositor
+       * grab) keeps its serial until it ends, but has no focus surface.
+       */
       if (touch_info->slot_serial == serial &&
+          touch_info->focus_surface &&
           touch_can_grab_surface (touch_info, surface))
         {
           if (sprite_out)
